<html>
<head>
	<meta content="text/html; charset=utf-8"/>
	<link rel="stylesheet" href=":/resources/cheatsheet/cheatsheet.css" type="text/css" />
</head>

<body>
	<h1>Segmentation Shape Interpolation</h1>

	<p><a href=#annotation_seg>Segmentation table view</a> | <a href=#pref_seg>Visibility preferences</a></p>
	<p><a href=#navi>Navigation preferences</a></p>

	<p>
	Paint an object on a few widely spaced slices and let KNOSSOS fill in everything between them.
	Paint a slice, move to another slice, paint it again — the shape in between is previewed
	continuously. Add as many slices as you like; each adjacent pair gets its own interpolation.
	Press Enter to commit the whole chain at once.
	</p>

	<p>
	The interpolation axis is fixed by the viewport you paint the first slice in: painting in
	<b>xy</b> interpolates along z, <b>xz</b> along y, <b>zy</b> along x. The status bar shows
	which plane the chain is in and how many key slices it has. The other two viewports show a
	cross-section through the whole chain, so you can watch the shape from the side as you build it.
	</p>

	<p>
	<b>Switching plane:</b> a chain belongs to one axis. While it has at most one key slice,
	painting in a different viewport simply moves it there. Once there are two or more, press
	Esc to end the chain first — the painted slices are kept either way.
	</p>

	<p>
	<b>Correcting an interpolated slice:</b> just paint or erase on it. The preview is baked
	into a real key slice on the first stroke, so you only have to touch the part that is wrong.
	</p>

	<p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th align="left">Shortcut</th><th align="left">Action</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tr><td><span class="sh"><img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/rightclick.png" alt="Right click"/></span></td><td>Paint on the current slice</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + <img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/leftclick.png" alt="Left click"/></span></td><td>Draw (alternative to right click; always paints, never erases)</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + <img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/rightclick.png" alt="Right click"/></span></td><td>Erase</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + <img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/middleclick.png" alt="Middle click"/> scroll</span></td><td>Change brush size</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh"><img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/middleclick.png" alt="Middle click"/> click</span></td><td>2D fill (stops at the edge of the loaded blocks)</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + <img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/middleclick.png" alt="Middle click"/> click</span></td><td>3D fill (always confined to the loaded blocks)</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">G</span></td><td>2D fill at the crosshair</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + G</span></td><td>3D fill at the crosshair</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Enter</span></td><td>Accept — write the interpolated volume</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Ctrl + P</span></td><td>Toggle interpolation preview</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Esc</span></td><td>End the current chain (painted slices are kept)</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">S</span></td><td>Toggle between Segmentation Paint and Shape Interpolation</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">&larr;</span></td><td>Jump to previous painted slice</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">&rarr;</span></td><td>Jump to next painted slice</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + &larr;</span></td><td>Jump to first painted slice</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Shift + &rarr;</span></td><td>Jump to last painted slice</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Delete</span> / <span class="sh">Backspace</span></td><td>Delete the painted slice at the current depth</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">D</span> / <span class="sh">F</span></td><td>Step one slice back / forward</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">-</span></td><td>Overlay: decrease opacity</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">+</span></td><td>Overlay: increase opacity</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh">Hold space</span></td><td>Reveal raw data temporarily</td></tr>
		<tr><td><span class="sh"><img src=":/resources/cheatsheet/leftclick.png" alt="Left click"/></span></td><td>Select object</td></tr>
	</table>
	</p>
</body>
</html>
